Here is a complete and simplified guide to **Tense in English Grammar** — very useful for **SSC CGL**, **RRB**, and other competitive exams.

---

## 🔹 **Tense** – काल (Kaal in Hindi)

Tense shows the **time of action** – when something happens.

### 🔸 3 Main Types of Tense:

1. **Present Tense** – वर्तमान काल
2. **Past Tense** – भूतकाल
3. **Future Tense** – भविष्यत काल

Each tense has **4 sub-types**, making a total of **12 tenses**.

---

## 📘 PRESENT TENSE

| Tense Type                     | Structure                          | Example                      |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| **Simple Present**             | Subject + V1 (+s/es)               | He plays cricket.            |
| **Present Continuous**         | Subject + is/am/are + V1 + ing     | He is playing cricket.       |
| **Present Perfect**            | Subject + has/have + V3            | He has played cricket.       |
| **Present Perfect Continuous** | Subject + has/have been + V1 + ing | He has been playing cricket. |

---

## 📕 PAST TENSE

| Tense Type                  | Structure                     | Example                      |
| --------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| **Simple Past**             | Subject + V2                  | He played cricket.           |
| **Past Continuous**         | Subject + was/were + V1 + ing | He was playing cricket.      |
| **Past Perfect**            | Subject + had + V3            | He had played cricket.       |
| **Past Perfect Continuous** | Subject + had been + V1 + ing | He had been playing cricket. |

---

## 📗 FUTURE TENSE

| Tense Type                    | Structure                           | Example                            |
| ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| **Simple Future**             | Subject + will/shall + V1           | He will play cricket.              |
| **Future Continuous**         | Subject + will be + V1 + ing        | He will be playing cricket.        |
| **Future Perfect**            | Subject + will have + V3            | He will have played cricket.       |
| **Future Perfect Continuous** | Subject + will have been + V1 + ing | He will have been playing cricket. |

---

## ✅ Helpful Tips:

* **V1 = base form** (play, eat)
* **V2 = past form** (played, ate)
* **V3 = past participle** (played, eaten)

